# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
/dist/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measured calibration data
#
# profiles/ holds real measurements of real hardware, including the device
# instance path of the machine that made them. It is per-operator data, it is
# recreated by running 'dovetail-diag calibrate', and a live build reads it
# from %LOCALAPPDATA%\Dovetail\profiles rather than from here anyway.
#
# The synthetic pair under tests/fixtures/profiles is deliberately NOT ignored:
# it is what selftest and stage5 run against on a clean machine.
#
# The FOLDER is kept and only its contents are ignored, which is load-bearing
# rather than cosmetic. ProfileStore.DevelopmentTree() identifies a build tree
# by an ancestor named 'src' with a 'profiles' folder beside it, and that is
# the signal that makes a dev run read the repository's own profiles instead of
# %LOCALAPPDATA%. Ignoring the directory outright removes the signal from a
# fresh clone, and stage5 fails on it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/profiles/*
!/profiles/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev-only harnesses and their output
#
# These drive the manual validation passes. They carry absolute host paths,
# they need a controller or a Windows Sandbox, and none of them is part of the
# shipped product. The automated suite is not here: selftest and stage5 are
# compiled into dovetail-engine and run in CI.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/artifacts/
/sandbox/
/_rollback/
attach-live-pass.ps1
record-live-pass.ps1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party reference material
#
# DS4Windows and x360ce source snapshots kept for comparison during the audit,
# plus _quarantined/, which holds an unsigned third-party DS4Windows rebrand of
# unestablished provenance. None of it is ours to redistribute and none of it
# is needed to build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/References/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source artwork
#
# assets/intro/ IS tracked: those renders are compiled into Dovetail.exe as WPF
# resources and the app will not build without them. What is ignored here is
# the raw source material they were cut from.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
assets/*.mp4
assets/*.jfif
assets/*.psd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
